2 It is prohibited to transfer funds to the natural persons, enterprises and organisations affected by the freeze or otherwise to make funds and economic resources available to them, directly or indirectly.

3 The prohibition under paragraph 2 does not apply to the provision of humanitarian aid and to the support of other activities that meet basic human needs by:
a. the United Nations, including its programmes, funds and other entities and bodies, and its specialised agencies and related organisations;
b. international organisations;
c. humanitarian organisations with observer status in the United Nations General Assembly and members of those organisations;
d. bilaterally or multilaterally funded non-governmental organisations participating in the United Nations humanitarian response plans, in refugee response plans, in other United Nations appeals or in humanitarian structures coordinated by the United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA);
e. the employees, grantees, subsidiaries or implementing partners of the organisations referred to in letters a−d, to the extent that they act in that capacity;
f. any other actors designated by the competent Committee of the United Nations Security Council.⁸

4 SECO may, by way of exception, authorise payments from frozen accounts, transfers of frozen assets and the release of frozen economic resources in order to:
a. avoid cases of hardship;
b. fulfil existing contracts;
c. satisfy claims that are the subject of an existing decision of a court, an administrative body or an arbitral tribunal;
d. meet humanitarian needs;
e. safeguard Swiss interests.⁹

5 It grants exceptions under paragraph 4 after consulting the competent units of the Eidgenössisches Departement für auswärtige Angelegenheiten and of the Eidgenössisches Finanzdepartement and, where applicable, after notifying the competent Committee of the United Nations Security Council and in accordance with that Committee's decisions and the relevant resolutions of the United Nations Security Council.¹⁰

